{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation complete (commit 125163c94d, Gerrit change 1447, awaiting votes).\n\nDiscipline: held-out TDD. 15-test oracle written and proven RED first (10 RED\nagainst name scaffolds, each for the right behavioral reason). Fixer implemented\nblind from the contract: 12/14 GREEN on first contact; the 2 failures were\noracle fixture defects (invalid tool arg killing the k-cycle run via retry\nexhaustion; wrong StepResult status/attr literals), not implementation bugs.\nAfter fixture fixes: 14/14. Mutation checks - each proved RED then restored:\n M1 key detection on run_step instead of calls -> both parallel arms RED\n M2 drop per-step memoisation -> memo cost test RED\n M3 hardcode 0.50 instead of call-time read -> threshold test RED\n M4 arm guard only under tool_step_limit -> 8 RED (primary verifier unprotected)\n M5 delete interpret_failure typed branch -> survived; oracle STRENGTHENED with\n    a 15th test pinning the runaway WARNING + counter merge, RED under M5.\n\nLive Bedrock proof (exp_k, haiku-4-5): genuine model-driven loop (bait tool +\nModelRetry landing rejection) aborted by the guard at 24 tool calls / 25\nrequests vs the 240-request burnout this bug shipped with; RunawayToolLoopError\npropagates UNWRAPPED through real Bedrock streaming; typed branch re-raises the\nsame object; WARNING names the runaway (never a provider outage); diagnostic is\ncontent-free (hashed signatures + counters only). Healthy arm: 30 distinct-arg\ncalls through the armed guard land normally, no Bedrock 400 (definitions stay\nadvertised).\n\nTimely live capture: the 8b97 close gate TODAY ran away exactly in this bug's\nblind spot - a 5-signature search_files k-cycle (max_consecutive_repeat=1,\ndistinct_ratio_window=0.208, five sigs x41 calls) burning all 240 requests\nbefore bounded recovery landed the verdict. The guard trips that run at ~24\ncalls.\n\nGates: lint clean, mypy clean (438 files), full marker suite matches the\npre-existing 6F/18E baseline exactly."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785978313219719001,"uuid":"8d6cd8a4-e557-4e2f-857c-13a8474eb06e"}